From: Thingino <dev@thingino.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: ingenic: allow the T31 pin-function shadow window

T31 muxes pins through the PZ shadow window at 0x7000 (GID2LD at
0x70f0), but t31_access_ranges only permits 0x0000-0x2ffc, so the
regmap rejects every shadow write. ingenic_shadow_config_pin() and
its load helper fail silently, no pin function is ever applied, and
the pins keep whatever the bootloader left. I2C0 PA12/13 stayed on
function 2 instead of function 1, so the SC2336 could not be reached.

Allow the window, as the X1000 table already does for its 0x700
shadow block.

---
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-ingenic.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/pinctrl-ingenic.c
@@ -2931,6 +2931,7 @@
 
 static const struct regmap_range t31_access_ranges[] = {
 	regmap_reg_range(0x0000, 0x3000 - 4),
+	regmap_reg_range(0x7000, 0x7000 + 0x100 - 4),
 };
 
 static const struct regmap_access_table t31_access_table = {
